    {
      "id": 200,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -600,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        540,
        760
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "What to download / where to put it",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 360 panorama from one photo - Qwen-Image 2.1 (2 passes, no green canvas) - EXPERIMENTAL\n\n> **Experimental, often incoherent.** Pass 1 (Qwen + pano360 LoRA) regularly invents volumes that make no sense around the photo (glass cylinders, stone pillars, doors stuck to columns). Pass 2 only fixes the left/right seam and the area behind the camera, not that. For a usable panorama, use **photo_to_pano360_klein** (fast) or **photo_to_pano360_krea2** (keeps the photo pixels).\n\n## Models (in `ComfyUI/models/`)\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/blob/main/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors) | `diffusion_models/` |\n| [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/blob/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors) | `text_encoders/` |\n| [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/blob/main/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors) | `vae/` |\n| [pano360_qwen21_edit_v1.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Gogodr/qwen-image-2.1-edit-pano360-lora/blob/main/pano360_qwen21_edit_v1.safetensors) | `loras/` |\n\nAny subfolder of `loras/` works: just select the file in the LoRA node.\n\n## Custom nodes (in `ComfyUI/custom_nodes/`)\n- **ComfyUI-PerspToERP** (180 degree roll for pass 2): https://github.com/shisa84/ComfyUI-PerspToERP\n\nRestart ComfyUI after installing.\n\n## Settings to adapt\n- **Input photo**: load your photo. It becomes the centre of the panorama.\n- **Scene** (pass 1): one sentence of about 15-35 words describing the whole place, then the lighting.\n- **Style only** (pass 2): materials, colours and light, no furniture words. **Back** (pass 2): \"The green area is ...\", what is behind the camera.\n- Output is 1536x768; 2048x1024 also works and is sharper, but slower.\n- The photo is regenerated by the model, not pasted back pixel for pixel.\n- Pass 2 turns the panorama by 180 degrees, paints the middle third green (what is behind the camera) and asks Qwen-Image 2.1 *without* the 360 LoRA to fill it, with a latent mask so nothing else changes. This removes the left/right seam. To skip it, bypass the pass 2 group and plug the pass 1 decode into the save.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
